## 3. Deployment Configuration

Jenkins connects to App Server 1 through SSH using the `tony` account.

Passwordless sudo was verified for the deployment commands.

The deployment script:

```bash
set -e

tar --exclude='.git' -czf /tmp/web-deployment.tar.gz -C "$WORKSPACE" .

scp /tmp/web-deployment.tar.gz tony@stapp01:/tmp/web-deployment.tar.gz

ssh tony@stapp01 "sudo -n tar -xzf /tmp/web-deployment.tar.gz -C /var/www/html && sudo -n chown -R sarah:sarah /var/www/html && sudo -n systemctl restart httpd && sudo -n rm -f /tmp/web-deployment.tar.gz"

rm -f /tmp/web-deployment.tar.gz
```

The script:
1. Archives the Jenkins workspace.
2. Excludes Git metadata.
3. Transfers the archive to App Server 1.
4. Extracts the application into `/var/www/html`.
5. Sets ownership to `sarah:sarah`.
6. Restarts Apache.
7. Removes the temporary deployment archive.

